# The Vistani women: Alenka, Mirabel, Sorvia (docs/voice/vistani_women.md)

~ start
if flag.vistani_met
Alenka [smile]: Back for more of our company? Sensible. It's the best in the valley, and the wine is still the worst.
-> menu
endif
set vistani_met
Narrator: Three women in layered skirts and a great deal of silver sit around a single candle, sharing one bottle and many opinions. They stop talking as you come over, which is how you know they were talking about you.
if flag.death_house_completed
Alenka [smile]: Sit, strangers. You came out of the house at the end of the lane. People don't. So: buy us a cup, and tell us how.
else
Alenka [smile]: Sit, strangers. New faces in Barovia! That happens about as often as sunshine. Buy us a cup and tell us everything.
endif
Mirabel [sly]: Or don't. We'll guess. Our guesses are always better than the truth.
Sorvia: Your boots have walked farther than boots should, in this valley. Sorry. I notice things.
-> menu

~ menu
* Who are you? -> who
* [if not flag.vistani_wine_bought and gold >= 3] Buy the table a bottle. (3 gp) -> wine
* What can you tell us about the man by the hearth? -> ismark
* What do you know about the burgomaster's daughter? -> ireena
* How does anyone get out of this valley? -> leave_valley
* What would you call us, then? -> nicknames
* [Insight DC 14] Watch how they watch you. -> insight_ok | insight_fail
* Read my palm. -> palm
* [if flag.madam_eva_rumor and not flag.eggs_sky_man_heard] Seen any other strangers come through? -> strangers
* [if flag.vistani_wine_bought and not flag.vistani_deck_tried] [Performance DC 13] Earn the next round: give them a song. -> perform_ok | perform_fail
* Goodbye. -> END

~ perform_ok
set vistani_deck_tried
Narrator: The song is old, the voice is willing, and by the second verse all three women are singing the parts you don't know.
Sorvia [smile]: You'll do. Here, take this. Our uncle won it, and lost it, and won it again. The pictures lie better than Mirabel.
Mirabel [sly]: Nobody lies better than Mirabel.
give deck_of_illusions
-> menu

~ perform_fail
set vistani_deck_tried
Narrator: The song falls flat somewhere around the chorus. Arik stops polishing a glass to watch it die.
Alenka: Brave. Very brave. Sit down before you hurt someone.
-> menu

# A wink (easter-egg plan R1, docs/story/eggs.md): the man the mists dropped out of the sky. Part one of three: Van
# Richten's jar and a leech at camp come later. Drafted by Gemini through the ai-bridge and edited
# (docs/plans/gemini_eggs/r1/); unvoiced.
~ strangers
set eggs_sky_man_heard
Alenka [smile]: Last spring a man came stumbling out of a turnip field with his eyebrows singed off. He swore a flying ship shaped like a great squid, big as a church, had fallen out of the sky with him aboard.
Mirabel [sly]: And that a little worm had crawled in through his eye to live behind his forehead and whisper to him. A strange tenant, and paying no rent at all.
Sorvia [sad]: I gave him a crust of bread. His eye did twitch when he thanked me, as if something in there was looking back.
Mirabel [smile]: It was a stye, little sister. A man will invent a whole fleet of flying sea-monsters before he admits to rubbing his eyes with dirty fingers.
Alenka: He walked off east toward Vallaki, still arguing with his own skull, and we never saw him again. The mists bring all sorts.
-> menu

~ who
set madam_eva_rumor
Alenka: Vistani. Our wagons go where they like; the mists open for us. Our camp is at Tser Pool, west along the road. Madam Eva keeps it. She reads the cards for strangers who ask nicely.
Mirabel: And for strangers who don't, she reads them anyway. It's worse.
-> menu

~ wine
gold -3
set vistani_wine_bought
Alenka [smile]: Generous! Arik, the good bottle. Yes, he has a good bottle. No, you've never seen it.
Sorvia: He knows you're here, you know. The lord. He knew before you did. He always does, because we...
Mirabel [angry]: Sorvia.
Sorvia: What? They'd work it out. They're not stupid. Look at them; they're nearly clever.
approve ratatoille +1 kip_smudgewick +1: You bought the Vistani's table a bottle
-> menu

~ ismark
set ismark_the_lesser_heard
Mirabel [sly]: Ismark the Lesser. His father was loud, and brave, and dead. Ismark is quiet, and brave, and not dead yet. Give him time.
Alenka: Be kind, Mirabel. He tips.
-> menu

~ ireena
Alenka: The burgomaster's daughter. Beautiful. Unlucky. The lord of the land has taken an interest. When he takes an interest, it's best to step aside.
Mirabel [sly]: Or to sell tickets.
Sorvia [sad]: She's nice. She mended my horse's bridle once and wouldn't take a copper. I hope... nothing. More wine?
-> menu

~ leave_valley
Alenka: The mists let us pass. Not you. Not anyone he hasn't finished with.
Sorvia: And he hasn't finished with you. He's hardly started.
interject tag:veteran: Good. Neither have we.
-> menu

~ nicknames
Mirabel [smile]: What would I call you? Oh, my sisters, listen to this, they want to be christened before they've even bought a round.
Mirabel [sly]: Hold still and let me look at the mud on your boots. A good name has to fit like a wet coat.
if class:paladin
Mirabel [sly]: You in the tin coat, you're "Kettle," because you shine like a scullery pot and you're already whistling at the boil.
endif
if class:cleric
Mirabel [smile]: And the soft one with the morning eyes is "Candle-end," still trying to light a whole church with an inch of tallow.
endif
if class:ranger
Mirabel [sly]: The one checking the floorboards for badger prints is "Bramble," all briar on the hem and nowhere to sit.
endif
if class:wizard
Mirabel [smile]: The fussy one smelling of sage and scorched paper is "Soup-bone," because they look like they'd lecture a turnip before peeling it.
endif
if class:monk
Mirabel [smile]: That little nimble thing is "Thimble," small enough to lose in a pocket and sharp enough to catch your thumb.
endif
if class:warlock
Mirabel [sly]: And you with the counting-house frown, you're "Farthing," always checking the rim to see who clipped you.
endif
Mirabel [sly]: Anyone left over gets "Pockets" until they do something worth a syllable. Don't look crestfallen, it's a perfectly dry name.
Mirabel [sad]: I called little Sorvia "Sparrow" when she started here. That is the only one I'd take back, if names came back.
-> menu

~ insight_ok
set vistani_spies_suspected
Narrator: Alenka's eyes keep returning to your weapons, your faces, the order you sit in. She isn't curious; she's taking inventory, for someone.
-> menu

~ insight_fail
Narrator: Three women enjoying an evening out. If they're anything more, the wine hides it.
-> menu

~ palm
Sorvia [smile]: Oh, yes! Give it here. Not you, Mirabel, I know yours; it says you'll die of being rude.
* [Fighter] Hold out a sword-callused palm. -> palm_fighter
* [Rogue] Offer a palm, keeping the other hand on your purse. -> palm_rogue
* [Cleric] Offer a palm, holy symbol and all. -> palm_cleric
* [Wizard] Offer an ink-stained palm. -> palm_wizard
* Offer a palm. -> palm_any
* Maybe later. -> menu

~ palm_fighter
Sorvia: Your life line is long. It's just that something keeps trying to cut it. There, see? Teeth marks.
-> menu

~ palm_rogue
Sorvia: This hand has been in a great many pockets. One of them belonged to someone very, very old. My advice? Give it back. Mirabel's advice will be to sell it.
Mirabel [sly]: Sell it.
-> menu

~ palm_cleric
Sorvia: A line of faith straight down the middle, and a crack right across it. Don't worry. Cracks let the light in, Grandmother says. Also the wind.
-> menu

~ palm_wizard
Sorvia: So many lines. You've read too much. One day a book is going to read you back.
interject name:ratatoille: That is not how books work. I'll have you know I have read hundreds, and not one has read me back.
-> menu

~ palm_any
Sorvia: You'll meet a tall, dark stranger. Everyone here does. Only once, usually.
-> menu
